Package: scoRch.generator
Title: Spatiotemporal Classification of Regional Compound Heatwaves
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Fawaz", "Bouhamad", email = "fawawaz@hotmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Nasser", "Najibi", role = "aut"))
Description: Detects local heatwaves in gridded daily maximum temperature,
    selects regionally extensive heatwave days, groups their heatwave cells
    with DBSCAN, fits principal-component ellipses with temperature-weighted
    centroids, classifies consecutive-day compound heatwave events into four
    space-time types, and fits the power-law and log-Gaussian Cox process
    models of the SCORCH method of Bouhamad and Najibi. One configuration
    file and one function run the complete workflow and write the catalogs,
    tables and descriptively named result plots.
